.TH SCRY 1 "July 2026" "Scry" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
scry \- fast terminal file browser, recursive finder, and SSH filesystem explorer

.SH SYNOPSIS
scry [OPTIONS] [PATH]
.nf
  -h, --help
      --manual
  -V, --version
      --generate-config
      --restore-session
      --ssh TARGET
      --preserve-hierarchy
  -a, --all
      --hidden-only
  -r, --recursive
      --fuzzy
      --query TEXT
      --files-only
      --dirs-only
  -T, --tree
      --no-open
      --exit-on-open
  -p, --permissions
  -s, --size
  -d, --date
  -u, --user
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBScry\fP is a fast, interactive terminal file browser, recursive finder, and SSH/SFTP filesystem explorer. It combines local and remote filesystem navigation with responsive \fBList\fP and \fBTree\fP views, live Exact and Fuzzy searching, structured query filters, detailed metadata inspection, and configurable terminal presentation.

\fBScry\fP is designed primarily as a keyboard-driven application, while also providing extensive mouse support. Files and directories may be browsed, searched, filtered, sorted, inspected, and opened without leaving the terminal interface. Optional metadata columns, file icons, information panels, themes, and persistent session restoration allow the browser to be adapted to different workflows and terminal environments.

Recursive searches run in the background and may operate across large directory trees. Queries can match filenames and complete relative paths, restrict results by file classification or extension, require or exclude terms, and use Boolean expressions with \fBAND\fP, \fBOR\fP, \fBNOT\fP, and parentheses. Exact and Fuzzy search modes may be combined with recursive scope and either \fBList\fP or \fBTree\fP presentation.

Remote filesystems may be browsed through OpenSSH and SFTP. \fBScry\fP supports saved connection profiles, persistent remote indexes, private local caching for opened files, transfer progress reporting, and SSH-only multi-file batch downloads. Remote directory hierarchies may either be flattened into the download destination or preserved when requested.

File opening, local deletion, session restoration, interface layout, startup modes, SSH behavior, and visual presentation may be controlled through command-line options and the \fBscry.toml\fP configuration file. Local deletion is optional and disabled by default.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print concise command-line help and exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-manual
Print the complete explanatory manual used by the in-app Help window and exit.

.TP
.BR \-v, " " \-\-version
Print the current version of \fBScry\fP and exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-generate\-config
Generate \fBscry.toml.generated\fP and exit.

The generated file must be reviewed and manually renamed to \fBscry.toml\fP before it becomes the active configuration. It is written to:
.nf

~/.config/scry/scry.toml.generated
.fi

.TP
.BR \-\-restore\-session
Restore the most recently saved browser session.

When session restoration is enabled, \fBScry\fP saves its current browser state during an orderly exit and restores it on a later destination-less launch. Restoration may be enabled through this option or by setting restore_settion = true in \fBscry.toml\fP. 

.TP
.BI "\-\-ssh " TARGET
Browse a remote filesystem through SSH/SFTP directly on startup.

\fBScry\fP connects immediately and opens the remote account's home directory unless a remote \fBPATH\fP is supplied.  Disconnect through the in-app SSH connection window opened with F4.

.TP
.BR \-\-preserve\-hierarchy
Preserve remote paths during marked batch downloads.

This option overrides the corresponding \fBscry.toml\fP setting for the current launch. Downloaded files retain paths relative to their remote locations instead of being gathered directly beneath the batch-download directory.

.TP
.BR \-a, " " \-\-all
Show hidden files and directories at startup.

.TP
.BR \-\-hidden\-only
Start with only hidden entries.

Restricts the visible results to hidden files, hidden directories, and all descendants beneath hidden directories.

.TP
.BR \-r, " " \-\-recursive
Start with a recursive listing.

Entries beneath the selected root are listed recursively, including descendants in nested directories. Enter a query in the search field fo filter the recursive result set.

.TP
.BR \-\-fuzzy
Start in Fuzzy search mode.

Fuzzy search mode will let you input approximate queries, such as, for example, \(lqhlep\(rq, to search for the word \(lqhelp\(rq. This is useful when the exact spelling of a target file or directory is unknown.

.TP
.BI "\-\-query " TEXT
Show TEXT in the search field at startup.

This allows a query to be supplied directly on the command line so matching results appear immediately after \fBScry\fP starts. Queries containing whitespace must me quoted by the shell.

.TP
.BR \-\-files\-only
Show files and symlinks only at startup.

Start \fBScry\fP with directories excluded from the visible result set. Files and symbolic links remain available until the filter is changed in-app or \fBScry\fP is launched without this option.

.TP
.BR \-\-dirs\-only
Show directories only at startup.

Start \fBScry\fP with non-directory entries excluded from the visible result set. This option cannot be combined with \fB\-\-files\-only\fP.

.TP
.BR \-T, " " \-\-tree
Start in \fBTree\fP mode.

\fBScry's Tree\fP mode offers an expandable and collapsible branched view of the file system. It provides a hierarchical overview in which directory branches may be expanded and collapsed. Directories open as branches revealing progressively deeper levels of the filesystem hierarchy. \fBTree\fP mode may also be restored through saved session state when session restoration is enabled by \fBscry.toml\fP or the command-line option.

.TP
.BR \-\-no\-open
Do not open selected files.

Directory navigation remains available, but activating a regular file will not launch an external opener.

.TP
.BR \-\-exit\-on\-open
Exit after successfully opening a file.

This option makes \fBScry\fP behave like a conventional chooser: after a regular file is opened successfully, \fBScry\fP exits immediately. Entering directories does not close the application, and a failed opener leaves \fBScry\fP running so the error remains visible.

.TP
.BR \-p, " "  \-\-permissions
Show permissions column at startup.

.TP
.BR \-s, " " \-\-size
Show size column at startup.

.TP
.BR \-d, " " \-\-date
Show date column at startup.

.TP
.BR \-u, " " \-\-user
Show user column at startup.


.\" Interactive Controls Section

.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
.TP
\fBScry\fP is designed for keyboard-first operation while retaining extensive mouse support. Most controls act immediately, and the footer displays contextual shortcuts for the current mode or open window.

.RE
.SS NAVIGATION
.TP
.BR Enter
.RS
Open the selected entry in \fBList\fP or \fBTree\fP mode, both locally and remotely. A selected directory is entered, while a selected file is opened. When a directory is selected in \fBTree\fP mode, establish that directory as the new browsing root. During an SSH session, Enter still activates a single, selected file, or enters the selected directory. Multiple files cannot be opened simultaneously.
.RE

.BR Up/Down
.RS
Move the selection by one entry.
.RE

.BR "Page Up/Page Down"
.RS
Move the selection by one visible page.
.RE

.BR Home/End
.RS
Select the first or last visible entry.
.RE

.BR Left/Escape
.RS
Move to the parent directory. In \fBTree\fP mode, collapse the selected branch or move the selection to its parent branch.
.RE

.BR Right
.RS
Enter the selected directory. In \fBTree\fP mode, expand the selected branch.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+T
.RS
Switch between \fBList\fP and \fBTree\fP views.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+C
.RS
Exit \fBScry\fP.
.RE

.SS "SEARCH AND QUERY EDITING"
.TP
.BR "Typing Printable Characters"
.RS
Insert text into the Search field and update the current result set.
.RE

.BR Backspace
.RS
Remove the character before the query caret.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+Left/Ctrl+Right
.RS
Move the query caret by one character.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+Home/Ctrl+End
.RS
Move the query caret to the beginning or end of the Search field.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+U
.RS
Clear the complete query.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+F
.RS
Switch between Exact and Fuzzy search modes.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+O
.RS
Cycle the active sort mode through Name, Size, Date, and Type.
.RE

.BR Alt+R
.RS
Toggle recursive searching beneath the current root.
.RE

.BR Ctrl+R
.RS
Reverse the current sort direction.
.RE

.RS
Search queries are evaluated as they are typed. Complete details of the compact and Boolean query languages are provided in the \fBSEARCHING\fP and \fBQUERY LANGUAGE\fP sections.
.RE

.RE
